-    "en": "Strict loss matching obeys the laws below on every frame (Becoming.LossMatching). On these laws FR proposes that, within an independently specified family of same-kind recoverable basic losses, a fixed graver loss should not retain sufficient priority over arbitrarily many fixed lesser basic protections solely through its gravity difference. Where support, burdens and historical conditions persist under scale expansion, some finite scale of joint protection should acquire sufficient grounds for choice. This is an additional normative candidate beyond LR’s neighborhood, with affirmative defense and author counterreview, not a consequence of existing axioms; the laws state its exact formal content, not its warrant. One repair process is an instance (laws 7–9).",
-    "zh": "严格损失匹配对每个框架服从下列规律（Becoming.LossMatching）。在这些规律之上，FR 提议：在独立说明的同类可恢复基本损失比较族中，固定的较重损失不应仅凭程度差异对任意多项固定的较轻基本保护始终保有充分优先；若支持、负担与历史条件可在规模扩展中保持，则某个有限共同保护规模应能取得充分选择根据。这是超出 LR 近邻的新增规范候选，附正面辩护与作者反审，不是已有公理的推论；规律陈述的是它的确切形式内容，不是它的根据。同一修复过程是实例（规律 7–9）。"
